It is done.

The Maw is quiet. The deep troll lies where it fell, and the mountain is already growing moss on it, because the mountain has seen bigger.

We built the new seal from the old one's rubble. Vala set the keystone. Thorin carved the word — deeper this time, so the next two hundred years have something to argue with. Muni stood in the gap while the mortar dried, out of habit, or maybe out of love.

Warden Dolgrim will limp for the rest of his days and refers to the limp as his trophy. The outer farms are already rebuilding; goblins burn faster than dwarves forget.

On the muster roll of the Third Seal, I have written three names. Vala added a fourth in her own hand, which is against regulation, and I have decided the regulation is wrong. Beside them, the oldest words we have:

DEBT PAID. DOOR HELD. ENOUGH.

— Brakka Stonewrit, Warden

